const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"联合比较而不是逐项贴标签",en:"Compare a profile rather than isolated ratios"},body:{zh:"Altman用多变量判别分析，将若干财务比率组合为区分两类企业的分数。重点在变量共同提供的信息，不是某个比率单独超过阈值就决定企业状况。一个单独区分能力较弱的变量，放入组合后仍可能有用，因此逐项排名不等于模型选择。",en:"Altman combines financial ratios to distinguish two predefined groups. The information in their joint profile matters, not a universal threshold on each ratio. A weak standalone discriminator may contribute when combined with other variables, so individual rankings do not reproduce model selection."},reference:{url:"https://calctopia.com/papers/Altman1968.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：1968年期刊版，第592–594页",en:"Source: 1968 journal article, pp. 592–594"}}},{title:{zh:"先看样本如何组成",en:"Begin with the sampling design"},body:{zh:"初始样本包含33家破产制造企业与33家非破产制造企业，后者按行业与规模进行配对选择。这样的研究设计有助于比较两类特征，却不等于现实市场中两类企业各占一半。阅读任何分类结果前，必须区分样本配比与总体发生率。",en:"The initial sample pairs 33 bankrupt manufacturers with 33 non-bankrupt manufacturers selected by industry and size. This supports comparison but does not imply equal prevalence in the market. Sample composition and population incidence must be distinguished before interpreting classification results."},reference:{url:"https://calctopia.com/papers/Altman1968.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：1968年期刊版，第593页",en:"Source: 1968 journal article, pp. 593"}}},{title:{zh:"五个比率衡量不同维度",en:"Five ratios represent different dimensions"},body:{zh:"模型包含营运资本、留存收益、息税前利润分别相对总资产的比率，以及股权市值相对债务账面价值、销售额相对总资产的比率。留存收益反映累计历史，并非当年利润；股权项使用市值而非账面权益。更换字段口径就已经改变了输入。",en:"Inputs cover working capital, retained earnings and EBIT relative to assets, market equity relative to book debt, and sales relative to assets. Retained earnings are cumulative, not annual income. The equity input uses market value, not book equity; substituting fields changes the model inputs."},reference:{url:"https://calctopia.com/papers/Altman1968.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：1968年期刊版，第594–595页",en:"Source: 1968 journal article, pp. 594–595"}}},{title:{zh:"系数大小不能直接解释重要性",en:"Coefficient size is not variable importance"},body:{zh:"作者从候选比率中反复比较组合，并明确不声称得到全局最优函数。不同输入的计量单位与波动大小不同，直接比较系数绝对值会误导。阅读或移植公式时，需要同时保留原始单位、尺度与完整变量组合，而不是挑出最大的系数。",en:"The variable set emerged from comparisons among alternatives, without a claim of global optimality. Different units and variability make raw coefficient magnitudes misleading. Reading or transferring the equation requires its input scales and full variable profile, not selection of the largest coefficient."},reference:{url:"https://calctopia.com/papers/Altman1968.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：1968年期刊版，第594–596页",en:"Source: 1968 journal article, pp. 594–596"}}},{title:{zh:"经营亏损不等于破产事件",en:"An operating loss is not a bankruptcy event"},body:{zh:"论文另外考察出现亏损但未破产的制造企业，提醒读者经营困难和法律上的破产不是同一标签。会计期间、报表取得时间与破产日期也不是同一时点。分类研究必须明确预测对象以及信息领先期，不能事后挑选最接近事件的一份资料冒充实时判断。",en:"A separate comparison considers loss-making manufacturers that did not fail. Operating difficulty and bankruptcy are different labels. Reporting periods, information availability and event dates also differ; a classification study needs an explicit target and lead time rather than a hindsight-selected statement."},reference:{url:"https://calctopia.com/papers/Altman1968.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：1968年期刊版，第593, 602页",en:"Source: 1968 journal article, pp. 593, 602"}}},{title:{zh:"判别分数不能读成概率",en:"A discriminant score is not a probability"},body:{zh:"Z在原文中是将变量压缩到一维的判别指标，不能把数值直接读成百分比风险。原样本的行业、规模和资料可得性也限制了外推。用于新的企业群体之前，应重新审视事件标签、样本分布和会计可比性，而不是只检查公式能否算出结果。",en:"Z is a one-dimensional discriminant index, not a percentage risk. Industry, size and data availability limit the original sample's reach. A new population requires reassessment of event definitions, sample distributions and accounting comparability, beyond checking that the equation can be computed."},reference:{url:"https://calctopia.com/papers/Altman1968.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：1968年期刊版，第592–593, 609页",en:"Source: 1968 journal article, pp. 592–593, 609"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"原研究以特定时期、可取得完整资料的制造业企业为样本。判别分数不是经过校准的破产概率，也不能不经重新检验直接套用到当代A股、金融企业或其他行业。",en:"The original sample covers manufacturers with sufficient historical data. A discriminant score is not a calibrated bankruptcy probability and cannot be transferred to present-day A-shares, financial firms or other sectors without validation."}};export{e as default};
